1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,959
Monday, nine in the morning. The pipeline is red, and nobody knows why.

2
00:00:05,509 --> 00:00:10,543
Three different people have three different theories. The code. The server. The password.

3
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:15,210
Here is the secret that experienced engineers share: they do not guess.

4
00:00:15,210 --> 00:00:16,718
They measure the pipeline,

5
00:00:16,718 --> 00:00:18,226
they read the first error,

6
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:19,733
and they change one thing.

7
00:00:20,283 --> 00:00:22,754
Today we measure our Cloud Cart pipeline.

8
00:00:22,754 --> 00:00:24,441
Then we break it three ways,

9
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:25,104
on purpose,

10
00:00:25,104 --> 00:00:26,129
and fix each one.

11
00:00:26,679 --> 00:00:30,497
And at the end, a script proves the whole domain. Prove the pipeline.

12
00:00:32,047 --> 00:00:33,476
Here is what to expect.

13
00:00:34,026 --> 00:00:36,565
One: the CI/CD domain, on one page.

14
00:00:37,115 --> 00:00:40,038
Two: the scenario, and the seven checks that prove it.

15
00:00:40,588 --> 00:00:41,872
Three: a live demo,

16
00:00:41,872 --> 00:00:44,305
in real Jenkins and a real terminal.

17
00:00:44,305 --> 00:00:45,049
We measure,

18
00:00:45,049 --> 00:00:45,657
we break,

19
00:00:45,657 --> 00:00:46,130
we fix,

20
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:47,009
and we prove.

21
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:51,698
Four: a short list of what to do when a check fails, and where to find the lab.

22
00:00:52,248 --> 00:00:55,384
This is the mastery lesson of the CI/CD domain.

23
00:00:56,934 --> 00:01:01,393
The CI/CD domain, on one page. Nine objectives, three lessons.

24
00:01:01,943 --> 00:01:05,002
Lesson one seventy-seven: what a pipeline is,

25
00:01:05,002 --> 00:01:05,750
its stages,

26
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:06,770
and build once,

27
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:07,653
promote many.

28
00:01:07,653 --> 00:01:09,421
The artifact is immutable,

29
00:01:09,421 --> 00:01:13,228
and the same file moves from dev to stage to production.

30
00:01:13,778 --> 00:01:17,074
Lesson one seventy-eight: gates that stop the line,

31
00:01:17,074 --> 00:01:18,883
secrets and least privilege,

32
00:01:18,883 --> 00:01:20,175
blue green releases,

33
00:01:20,175 --> 00:01:20,757
rollback,

34
00:01:20,757 --> 00:01:21,532
smoke tests,

35
00:01:21,532 --> 00:01:22,695
and notifications.

36
00:01:23,245 --> 00:01:25,571
Today: reliability and troubleshooting,

37
00:01:25,571 --> 00:01:26,704
and then the proof.

38
00:01:26,704 --> 00:01:27,599
Two objectives,

39
00:01:27,599 --> 00:01:28,493
eight and nine.

40
00:01:29,043 --> 00:01:33,665
Reliability means two numbers you can measure: how often the pipeline succeeds,

41
00:01:33,665 --> 00:01:34,953
and how long it takes.

42
00:01:35,503 --> 00:01:38,447
Troubleshooting means one habit: read the first error.

43
00:01:39,997 --> 00:01:40,851
The scenario.

44
00:01:40,851 --> 00:01:42,429
The Cloud Cart pipeline,

45
00:01:42,429 --> 00:01:43,809
delivered and proven.

46
00:01:43,809 --> 00:01:44,663
Seven checks,

47
00:01:44,663 --> 00:01:45,714
run by a script.

48
00:01:46,264 --> 00:01:47,567
One: Jenkins is up,

49
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:48,937
and both jobs exist.

50
00:01:48,937 --> 00:01:50,925
Two: the last build is green,

51
00:01:50,925 --> 00:01:52,707
and it ran the smoke test.

52
00:01:53,257 --> 00:01:56,577
Three: the release in Nexus matches its checksum.

53
00:01:56,577 --> 00:01:57,254
Four: dev,

54
00:01:57,254 --> 00:01:59,422
stage and production all answer.

55
00:01:59,972 --> 00:02:03,286
Five: production runs a version that is in Nexus.

56
00:02:03,286 --> 00:02:04,976
Six: a rollback is ready,

57
00:02:04,976 --> 00:02:07,140
with two releases and two sides.

58
00:02:07,690 --> 00:02:09,518
Seven: no password in the code.

59
00:02:09,518 --> 00:02:10,933
That last one is a trap,

60
00:02:10,933 --> 00:02:12,938
and we will fall in it on purpose.

61
00:02:13,488 --> 00:02:18,843
Besides the checks, the script measures the pipeline: success rate, and average duration.

62
00:02:19,393 --> 00:02:23,297
The script checks facts, not your word. Seven of seven is mastery.

63
00:02:24,847 --> 00:02:25,660
Real Jenkins,

64
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:28,349
and the pipeline from the last two lessons.

65
00:02:28,349 --> 00:02:30,538
Today we do not build anything new.

66
00:02:30,538 --> 00:02:31,413
We measure it,

67
00:02:31,413 --> 00:02:32,164
we break it,

68
00:02:32,164 --> 00:02:33,039
and we fix it.

69
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:36,294
First,

70
00:02:36,294 --> 00:02:36,835
measure.

71
00:02:36,835 --> 00:02:38,861
This is the Cloud Cart CI job.

72
00:02:38,861 --> 00:02:39,672
On the left,

73
00:02:39,672 --> 00:02:42,104
the build history lists every build.

74
00:02:42,104 --> 00:02:43,388
Green is a success,

75
00:02:43,388 --> 00:02:44,806
and red is a failure.

76
00:02:45,356 --> 00:02:46,398
Now the terminal.

77
00:02:46,398 --> 00:02:49,399
Lab up checks that Jenkins and Nexus are running,

78
00:02:49,399 --> 00:02:51,543
and says where the results will go.

79
00:02:52,093 --> 00:02:56,765
Lab stats counts the history for us. Four builds. One red, and three green.

80
00:02:57,315 --> 00:02:59,562
Success rate: seventy-five percent.

81
00:02:59,562 --> 00:03:02,322
Average duration: well under half a minute.

82
00:03:02,322 --> 00:03:04,568
Those two numbers are the baseline.

83
00:03:05,118 --> 00:03:06,235
When the rate drops,

84
00:03:06,235 --> 00:03:07,239
or the time grows,

85
00:03:07,239 --> 00:03:08,244
something changed.

86
00:03:08,244 --> 00:03:09,304
And you can see it,

87
00:03:09,304 --> 00:03:10,644
before anyone complains.

88
00:03:11,194 --> 00:03:16,527
And where does the time go? In Jenkins, the stages view shows the time of every stage.

89
00:03:22,477 --> 00:03:23,295
Failure one.

90
00:03:23,295 --> 00:03:23,976
Last week,

91
00:03:23,976 --> 00:03:27,382
a teammate changed the deployer password in Nexus,

92
00:03:27,382 --> 00:03:29,767
and typed the old one into Jenkins.

93
00:03:29,767 --> 00:03:30,789
Nobody noticed.

94
00:03:30,789 --> 00:03:33,037
Today a developer starts a build.

95
00:03:33,587 --> 00:03:36,510
In Jenkins, we open the job, and click Build Now.

96
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,374
We open the stages view.

97
00:03:52,424 --> 00:03:52,691
Red,

98
00:03:52,691 --> 00:03:54,024
at Publish to Nexus.

99
00:03:54,024 --> 00:03:55,491
Build and test passed,

100
00:03:55,491 --> 00:03:56,824
so the code is fine.

101
00:03:56,824 --> 00:04:00,424
The pipeline stopped at the stage that talks to Nexus.

102
00:04:08,274 --> 00:04:10,941
We open the console, and we read the first error.

103
00:04:17,091 --> 00:04:18,682
Status code four oh one,

104
00:04:18,682 --> 00:04:19,544
Unauthorized.

105
00:04:19,544 --> 00:04:21,666
Nexus does not know who this is.

106
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:22,925
It is not the code,

107
00:04:22,925 --> 00:04:24,450
and it is not the role.

108
00:04:24,450 --> 00:04:25,710
It is the password.

109
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:31,822
In Jenkins, a password lives in one place: Credentials.

110
00:04:36,672 --> 00:04:39,080
We open the nexus deployer entry.

111
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:39,955
On the page,

112
00:04:39,955 --> 00:04:43,530
Jenkins even lists where it was used: the CI job,

113
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:44,332
build five,

114
00:04:44,332 --> 00:04:44,843
in red.

115
00:04:50,093 --> 00:04:53,122
We click Update credential, and then Change Password.

116
00:05:01,472 --> 00:05:06,080
And we replace the old dots with the right password. It stays hidden, as it should.

117
00:05:06,630 --> 00:05:07,484
Then Save.

118
00:05:11,434 --> 00:05:13,546
Back to the job, and Build Now again.

119
00:05:22,396 --> 00:05:27,878
The stages view. Green, all the way. One cause, and one fix. We never touched the code.

120
00:05:59,728 --> 00:06:00,525
Failure two.

121
00:06:00,525 --> 00:06:03,514
A tired engineer promotes a version to stage,

122
00:06:03,514 --> 00:06:04,577
and mistypes it.

123
00:06:04,577 --> 00:06:06,171
We open the promote job.

124
00:06:12,421 --> 00:06:13,722
Build with Parameters.

125
00:06:17,272 --> 00:06:19,320
Version one point oh point thirty-three.

126
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:22,598
Target, stage. And Build.

127
00:06:29,148 --> 00:06:30,343
The stages view.

128
00:06:37,093 --> 00:06:39,376
Red, at Release. We open the console.

129
00:06:48,626 --> 00:06:49,697
Download failed.

130
00:06:49,697 --> 00:06:52,508
Nexus answered four oh four for that file.

131
00:06:52,508 --> 00:06:53,178
Not found.

132
00:06:53,178 --> 00:06:54,584
It is not a password,

133
00:06:54,584 --> 00:06:56,391
and it is not a permission.

134
00:06:56,391 --> 00:06:58,332
The file is simply not there.

135
00:07:00,882 --> 00:07:05,042
We do not guess. In the terminal, we ask Nexus which versions exist.

136
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:07,136
One point oh point one,

137
00:07:07,136 --> 00:07:07,539
three,

138
00:07:07,539 --> 00:07:07,875
four,

139
00:07:07,875 --> 00:07:08,412
and six.

140
00:07:08,412 --> 00:07:10,090
There is no thirty-three.

141
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:12,910
The engineer meant one point oh point six.

142
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:16,446
So we run the promote job again, with the right version.

143
00:07:22,596 --> 00:07:23,898
Build with Parameters.

144
00:07:27,448 --> 00:07:29,282
Version one point oh point six.

145
00:07:31,032 --> 00:07:32,760
Target, stage. And Build.

146
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:42,097
The stages view. Green. Failure two, fixed.

147
00:07:52,447 --> 00:07:53,333
Failure three.

148
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:56,750
The machine of the dev server was restarted overnight,

149
00:07:56,750 --> 00:07:59,091
and the dev Tomcat did not come back.

150
00:07:59,091 --> 00:08:00,103
In the terminal,

151
00:08:00,103 --> 00:08:01,748
we ask dev for its health.

152
00:08:02,298 --> 00:08:04,709
Not found. Nothing answers on that port.

153
00:08:05,259 --> 00:08:08,246
Now a developer builds. In Jenkins, Build Now.

154
00:08:18,496 --> 00:08:19,690
The stages view.

155
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:33,215
Build and test: green. Publish to Nexus: green. Red, only at Deploy to dev.

156
00:09:12,265 --> 00:09:17,982
The console. Verify failed. No answer on port ninety one oh one. Is Tomcat running?

157
00:09:26,632 --> 00:09:28,402
The file is safe in Nexus.

158
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:30,989
Only the last mile failed: the server.

159
00:09:30,989 --> 00:09:32,691
So the fix is the server.

160
00:09:33,241 --> 00:09:35,524
In the terminal, we start the dev Tomcat.

161
00:09:38,074 --> 00:09:40,826
And we ask dev for its health again. It answers.

162
00:09:41,376 --> 00:09:43,360
Back to Jenkins, and Build Now.

163
00:09:53,510 --> 00:09:59,120
The stages view. Green. Three failures, three different places, and three small fixes.

164
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:25,702
Now the proof. In the terminal, lab check.

165
00:10:33,752 --> 00:10:37,443
Six pass. One fails: a password in the code. We will fix it.

166
00:10:37,993 --> 00:10:38,694
Which file?

167
00:10:38,694 --> 00:10:39,458
We ask grep,

168
00:10:39,458 --> 00:10:41,880
and it names it: an old deploy script,

169
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,791
with a password in plain text.

170
00:10:43,791 --> 00:10:45,957
A script from before the pipeline,

171
00:10:45,957 --> 00:10:47,550
forgotten in the project.

172
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:52,324
We treat it as leaked. First, we remove the file, and we commit the change.

173
00:10:54,874 --> 00:10:56,470
Removing is not enough.

174
00:10:56,470 --> 00:10:57,996
Git keeps the history,

175
00:10:57,996 --> 00:11:01,118
so the old password must be changed in Nexus,

176
00:11:01,118 --> 00:11:03,130
as in lesson one seventy-six.

177
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:06,347
Lab check, one more time. Seven of seven.

178
00:11:06,897 --> 00:11:08,873
Results are part of the mastery.

179
00:11:08,873 --> 00:11:10,849
The script saved them in a file.

180
00:11:10,849 --> 00:11:11,405
Print it.

181
00:11:11,405 --> 00:11:12,764
This is your evidence.

182
00:11:13,314 --> 00:11:14,641
And lab stats again.

183
00:11:14,641 --> 00:11:15,769
Eight builds now.

184
00:11:15,769 --> 00:11:16,499
Five green.

185
00:11:16,499 --> 00:11:17,429
The rate fell,

186
00:11:17,429 --> 00:11:20,150
because we broke the pipeline on purpose,

187
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:22,274
and the numbers say so honestly.

188
00:11:22,824 --> 00:11:23,167
Last,

189
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:23,991
the cleanup.

190
00:11:23,991 --> 00:11:26,599
Lab down keeps a copy of the evidence,

191
00:11:26,599 --> 00:11:28,796
and removes the temporary files.

192
00:11:28,796 --> 00:11:29,345
Jenkins,

193
00:11:29,345 --> 00:11:29,757
Nexus,

194
00:11:29,757 --> 00:11:31,816
the jobs and the servers stay.

195
00:11:31,816 --> 00:11:36,072
And it reminds us: change any password we typed in plain text.

196
00:11:36,622 --> 00:11:41,315
Measured, broken, fixed, proved, written down, and cleaned up. That is mastery.

197
00:11:42,865 --> 00:11:45,809
When the pipeline fails, the stage tells you where to look.

198
00:11:46,359 --> 00:11:50,754
Red at Publish, four oh one: the credential. Fix it in Jenkins, once.

199
00:11:51,304 --> 00:11:56,573
Red at Release, four oh four: the version does not exist. Ask Nexus which ones do.

200
00:11:57,123 --> 00:12:01,667
Red at Deploy, no answer: the server is down. Start it, then build again.

201
00:12:02,217 --> 00:12:06,164
Red at Build and test: the code. Read the name of the failing test.

202
00:12:06,714 --> 00:12:09,679
And a password in the code: remove it, and change it.

203
00:12:11,229 --> 00:12:14,024
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

204
00:12:14,574 --> 00:12:22,808
One: the repository, github.com/it-waves/devops-ai, in the folder academy/lab.

205
00:12:23,358 --> 00:12:29,609
Two: the files, lab179.sh and shortcuts179.sh.

206
00:12:30,159 --> 00:12:35,834
Three: load the short names with source shortcuts179.sh. Then lab up.

207
00:12:36,384 --> 00:12:39,007
Four: lab check runs the seven checks.

208
00:12:39,007 --> 00:12:41,216
Lab stats measures the pipeline.

209
00:12:41,216 --> 00:12:42,528
Lab down cleans up.

210
00:12:43,078 --> 00:12:47,167
Five: you need the Jenkins and Nexus from the earlier lessons.

211
00:12:47,167 --> 00:12:49,740
Set your Jenkins login in JENKINS_AUTH,

212
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:53,104
and your deployer in NEXUS_USER and NEXUS_PASSWORD.

213
00:12:53,654 --> 00:12:55,297
The link is in the description.

214
00:12:56,847 --> 00:12:58,618
Your turn, on your own machine.

215
00:12:59,168 --> 00:13:03,904
One: lab up, then lab stats. Write down your success rate, and your average time.

216
00:13:04,454 --> 00:13:10,022
Two: put a wrong password in Jenkins credentials. Build, read the four oh one, and fix it.

217
00:13:10,572 --> 00:13:13,404
Three: promote a version that does not exist,

218
00:13:13,404 --> 00:13:15,041
and read the four oh four.

219
00:13:15,041 --> 00:13:16,237
Then stop a Tomcat,

220
00:13:16,237 --> 00:13:16,615
build,

221
00:13:16,615 --> 00:13:18,252
and read the verify error.

222
00:13:18,802 --> 00:13:20,920
Four: plant a password in a script.

223
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:22,312
Lab check will find it.

224
00:13:22,312 --> 00:13:22,917
Remove it,

225
00:13:22,917 --> 00:13:24,370
and change the password.

226
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:28,760
Five: lab check, until you see seven of seven. Then lab down.

227
00:13:29,310 --> 00:13:31,038
Pause the video, and do it now.

228
00:13:46,588 --> 00:13:47,463
Quick check.

229
00:13:48,013 --> 00:13:52,173
Red at Publish with four oh one: do you change the code, or the credential?

230
00:13:52,723 --> 00:13:55,517
A promote says four oh four. What do you do first?

231
00:13:56,067 --> 00:13:58,009
Which two numbers measure a pipeline?

232
00:13:58,559 --> 00:14:02,121
A password was committed once, then removed. Is it safe now?

233
00:14:02,671 --> 00:14:07,706
Objectives covered: CI/CD Engineering mastery. The whole domain, proved.

234
00:14:08,256 --> 00:14:10,325
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

235
00:14:20,875 --> 00:14:25,014
Next: a new domain. GitHub Actions, where your code builds itself.

236
00:14:25,564 --> 00:14:28,892
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
